{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as mopho/tg55. Rows follow the Muse panel: voice control (timbre volume/pan/spread, glide, detune, unison/mono) + global output/clock -> oscillators 1 & 2 (FM + sync switches) -> modulation oscillator (with its routing buttons) + mixer -> filters 1 & 2 -> filter / VCA envelopes -> LFO 1+2, pitch LFO, arpeggiator -> diffusion delay (global) + performance controllers. All timbre groups share one select (select.shared = 'timbre'): A / B, 'both' writes both; B edits go out on the MULTI IN B channel (muse.json driverNotes). Only CC-mapped controls exist: no main/headphone volume, envelope curves, mod map, chord, voice count, sequencer steps. All values 7-bit; enum values are CC bands (muse.json 'wire'). The mod-osc routing buttons (pitch/pwm -> osc 1/2, filter 1/2, pan) and filter 1 HIGH PASS are knobs here because the chart gives them 0-127, not on/off.",
